================================================================================

SCOPE — what this licence does and does not cover

This licence applies to the SOURCE CODE and DOCUMENTATION in this
repository: the Python modules under core/, screens/, tools/ and main.py,
the JSON configuration and layout files, and the Markdown documents.

It does NOT apply to:

  Artwork derived from Master of Orion 2
      Portraits, banners, planets, nebulae, backgrounds and icons under
      screens/*/assets/ and assets/shared/ are derived
      from the artwork of Master of Orion 2: Battle at Antares
      (Simtex / MicroProse, 1996). Copyright in the underlying work
      remains with its rightsholder. They are included here as part of a
      modification that requires an installed, legally obtained copy of
      the game and replaces none of it. They are not licensed for reuse
      outside that purpose, and no claim of ownership is made over them.

  AI-generated artwork
      The planet surface sheet
      screens/colony_summary/assets/_src/surfaces/planet_surfaces.png and
      the ten tiles tools/make_surface_tiles.py cuts from it, and the
      output-panel icon sheets under
      screens/colony_summary/assets/_src/output/ with the icons cut from
      them, were generated by the maintainer with ChatGPT. No copyright is
      claimed over them.

      The HUD, assets/shared/hud/galaxy_hud.png, and the pieces
      tools/hud_cut.py cuts from it, and the maintainer's galaxy screen
      mockup (work order 169; kept with the developer's records, not in
      this repository since work order 189), are AI-generated by the
      maintainer. No copyright is claimed over them.
      The button glyphs tools/hud_glyphs.py draws into the same folder
      (work order 179) are not cut from it and not AI-generated: they are
      drawn from coordinates written by hand in
      assets/shared/hud/glyphs.json, take nothing from a MOO2 file, and
      are part of this project's source under its licence.

      The universal background, assets/shared/backgrounds/universal.png,
      is the maintainer's, delivered on 29 September 2026 as
      univeral.png (sha256 97d29c29541ca14b...) and committed byte for
      byte (work order 191); it replaces the first one, delivered on 25
      September 2026 as background_univeral.png (sha256
      65e4421c2f67182c..., work order 173). How they were made is not
      recorded in the tree. No copyright is claimed over them.
      Two cockpit frames are AI-generated as well, which this file did
      not say until work order 169 (work order 168 found it): the galaxy
      map's frame, built from a ChatGPT render, and the Fleets screen's,
      an AI draft edited and upscaled by the maintainer, with the
      research panel's frame cut from it. No copyright is claimed over
      them. The other cockpit frames (the colony summary's, the planets
      screen's and the GAME menu's) are the maintainer's; how they were
      made is not recorded. None of the frames is drawn since decision
      71, and none is in the tree any more: work orders 189 and 190
      removed them (the history keeps them).

  The display font
      assets/shared/fonts/Aldrich-Regular.ttf is Copyright (c) 2011
      Matthew Desmond (MADType) and is licensed under the SIL Open Font
      License, Version 1.1 — see assets/shared/fonts/OFL.txt.

  Anything extracted at runtime
      Context-help texts (HELP.LBX) and nebula reference sprites
      (STARBG.LBX) are read from the user's own installation by
      tools/help_extract.py and tools/nebula_extract.py. They are not
      part of this repository and are excluded by .gitignore.

OrionLayer requires orion2re, a separate project, to run. It communicates
with it over a local TCP socket and includes no part of it.
